## Review scoring rules

### Input — each review arrives with this schema

```json
{
  "review_id":             "string — unique identifier",
  "position":              "integer — order in the list (1 = most recent)",
  "rating":                "integer — 1 to 5",
  "snippet":               "string — review text",
  "snippet_length":        "integer — character count of snippet",
  "author_name":           "string",
  "author_reviews_count":  "integer — total reviews by this author on Google Maps",
  "author_photos_count":   "integer — total photos uploaded by this author",
  "is_local_guide":        "boolean",
  "images_count":          "integer — photos attached to this review",
  "response_present":      "boolean — owner replied to this review",
  "was_edited":            "boolean — review was modified after posting",
  "likes":                 "integer — helpful votes from other users"
}
```

### Output — for each review return a scored object

Add `score_breakdown` to each review. Include **only non-zero criteria** in `score_breakdown`.

```json
{
  "review_id": "string",
  "rating": "integer (1–5)",
  "author_name": "string",
  "score_breakdown": {
    "THIN_ACCOUNT_1": 10,
    "SHORT_TEXT": 10,
    "GENERIC_TEXT": 20,
    "FIVE_STAR_EMPTY": 15,
    "EXPERIENCED_AUTHOR_5": -10
  }
}
```

---

### Scoring table

Score each review individually. Sum all matching criteria. The total score determines the label.
Use the `key` as the field name in `score_breakdown`.

### Fake signals — add points

| Key                   | Criterion                                                                                   | Points |
|-----------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|--------|
| `THIN_ACCOUNT_0`      | `author_reviews_count` = 0–1                                                               | +20    |
| `THIN_ACCOUNT_1`      | `author_reviews_count` = 2–3                                                               | +10    |
| `SHORT_TEXT_EXTREME`  | `snippet_length` < 20 characters                                                            | +25    |
| `SHORT_TEXT`          | `snippet_length` < 60 characters                                                            | +10    |
| `BURST_AFTER_NEGATIVE`| Post-negative burst — 5★ review appears immediately after a 1–2★ review                    | +20    |
| `FIVE_STAR_EMPTY`     | 5★ rating AND `snippet_length` < 50 characters                                              | +15    |
| `SURNAME_REPEAT`      | Repeated surname — reviewer shares last name with one or more others                        | +20    |
| `GENERIC_TEXT`        | Generic text / no specifics — no mention of staff, product, price, time, or concrete detail | +20    |
| `SUSPICIOUS_NEGATIVE` | 1–2★ AND any of: `snippet_length` < 50 OR `author_reviews_count` = 0–1 OR `BURST_AFTER_NEGATIVE` OR `GENERIC_TEXT` | +20 |
| `MARKETING_TONE`      | Emotional or marketing tone — "best ever", "incredible", "unique offer"                     | +10    |
| `EMOJI_SPAM`          | Excessive punctuation or emoji — `!!!`, `🔥🔥🔥`, purely decorative, no substance          | +10    |
| `TEMPLATE_CLONE`      | Template clone — phrasing or structure nearly identical to another review                   | +20    |

### Real signals — subtract points

| Key                   | Criterion                                                                                   | Points |
|-----------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|--------|
| `EDITED_REVIEW`       | Review was edited after posting (`was_edited` = true)                                       | −15    |
| `HAS_PHOTOS`          | Review includes photos (`images_count` > 0)                                                 | −20    |
| `EXPERIENCED_AUTHOR_5`| `author_reviews_count` > 5                                                                  | −10    |
| `EXPERIENCED_AUTHOR_10`| `author_reviews_count` > 10                                                                | −15    |
| `ACTIVE_PROFILE`      | `author_photos_count` > 5 — active account with photo history                              | −10    |
| `LONG_TEXT`           | `snippet_length` > 150 characters                                                           | −20    |
| `SPECIFIC_DETAILS`    | Specific details — names, products, prices, waiting times, physical descriptions            | −20    |
| `BALANCED_TONE`       | Balanced tone — review mentions both positives and negatives or caveats                     | −15    |
| `NATURAL_LANGUAGE`    | Natural imperfect language — typos, colloquialisms, personal voice                          | −10    |
| `LOCAL_GUIDE`         | `is_local_guide` = true — Google-verified active contributor                                | −15    |
| `OWNER_RESPONDED`     | `response_present` = true — business responded, suggests real interaction                   | −10    |
| `HELPFUL_VOTES`       | `likes` > 0 — other users marked the review as helpful                                     | −10    |

### Rules

- apply this scoring to every review. Include `score_breakdown` (using the keys above) for each.
- processed_reviews must include every review from the input.
